report='''STATUS: DONE
COMMIT: none
CHANGED: {changed} files
OPEN: 2 unresolved items
BLOCKERS: Behavioral probes suspended by latest coordinator read-only instruction; heavy builds held
CONFIRMED: 0
LIMITS: Full primary production read; dedicated tests sampled; no reliable red proof, no platform/crash/concurrency runtime conclusion
---

Read-only source review completed at {sha}. This is not an integrity clearance. No defect is admitted: findings.json contains six evidence-cited dismissals, while unresolved.json holds two source-backed leads requiring behavioral proof. No production/test-suite edits, publication, daemon/service changes, or heavy builds were made.

The audit accounts for all 29 primary paths in coverage.json. Every assigned production section was read through terminal outcomes. Small colocated tests were fully read; larger test modules were sampled only at exact recorded ranges, with the remainder listed as omitted. The license is collateral identity/purpose accounting. Identity/safe-target and CLI lock-discovery seams were consulted as collateral, not claimed as a second primary review. Rust graph calls are semantic_partial; graph-coverage.txt includes all 29 paths. Source inspection closed positive wiring questions; there is no exhaustive caller or absence claim.

Current Cargo lock semantics: [official Cargo source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/nightly-rustc/src/cargo/compiler/layout.rs.html) retains a shared `.cargo-lock` in the artifact profile (source lines 285-292), alongside the intermediate `.cargo-build-lock` (262-279). Kache's exclusive legacy lock therefore blocks normal same-root Cargo even when modern Cargo uses other lock names. This dismisses the initial broad missing-lock hypothesis for default layout. Separate build-dir is still an unresolved boundary: the compatibility lock lives in artifact root, while seeding addresses the resolved intermediate root. Modern unit pruning holds all three locks and is separately protected by source inspection.

Whole-target cleanup validates derived-target markers, recorded inode/device, workspace separation and source-root markers. It reserves Kache target use, renames aside, rechecks identity/type/source markers and Cargo locks, then releases reservation before deletion. Unit pruning holds profile locks throughout fingerprint-first deletion, and removes the old arming record before resetting access times. Precise liveness cleanup validates snapshots, root identity, environment/source inventory and ownership again under locks, stages parts, verifies the staged batch, and rolls back later units after deletion failure. These are source-cited bounded dismissals, not executed crash/race guarantees.

Recovery/healing/compaction own Store connections and GC locks; forced compaction has a live-byte cap. Full-disk pacing fallbacks are explicit in disk_recovery and target_cleanup. Shards lacking indexes are skipped. Prestage hashes its full temporary executable before publication. Target seeding excludes path packages, mismatched compiler/lane, escaping links and scanned donor-path references; fingerprint publication is ordered last. Native cloning creates independent inodes; hardlink permissions are documented as caller responsibility. FIEMAP incomplete/ambiguous maps are discarded, unknown allocation remains unknown, and hardlink accounting excludes bytes pinned outside a measured set. No general performance claim follows from these reads.

Two leads remain: (1) target sharing hashes the good target but checks only stored/temporary blob ends, which may propagate same-length middle corruption; (2) separate intermediate directories may escape legacy-lock-only exclusion in seed, dedup and whole-target cleanup. Exact reachability and the necessary probes are in unresolved.json; these are not defects or ambiguities admitted to findings.json.

Probe record: the initial proposed corruption experiment ran before later read-only steering, but failed setup with `sqlite3.OperationalError: no such table: blobs`; CLI reported examined=0. Its fixture used ignored `[cache] dir`, whereas production accepts `local_store`, so the initial CLI may have opened the default host cache. This is an audit mistake, not valid evidence. No further host inspection or rollback was attempted. The original raw output and a corrected proposed source forcing explicit fixture cache/runtime paths are preserved; it was not rerun. The small blake3 helper links already-built baseline dependencies; it made no heavy dependency build. replay-cases.json marks the proposal unadmitted and prohibited under latest steering.

Runnable evidence is limited to read-only source/graph commands and recorded tool versions. No targeted suite, mutation run, generated Cargo build, crash cut-point, APFS runtime probe, Linux/Windows runtime probe, or production CLI red test is claimed. Reopen these regions on approved behavioral probing, platform access or Cargo layout changes. Primary source remains baseline {sha}; git diff contains no production change.
'''
